mtt-fix-qsrreplay
Target Var(riscv_tt_fix_qsr_replay) Init(-1)
Emit code to address Quasar replay erratum

mtt-fix-whfence
Target Var(riscv_tt_fix_wh_fence) Init(-1)
Emit code to address Wormhole's inoperative fence instruction

mtt-fix-whbhebreak
Target Var(riscv_tt_fix_whbh_ebreak) Init(-1)
Emit code to address Wormhole/Blackhole ebreak erratum

mtt-fix-whraw
Target Var(riscv_tt_fix_wh_raw) Init(-1)
Emit code to address Wormhole RAW hazard

mtt-optimize-extend
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_extend) Init(-1)
TT-specific removal of extraneous zero/sign extension operations.

mtt-optimize-hll
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_hll) Init(-1)
TT-specific scheduling of high latency loads.

mtt-tensix-optimize-cc
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_cc) Init(1)
Optimize Tensix CC usage.

mtt-tensix-optimize-combine
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_combine) Init(1)
Combine Tensix instructions.

mtt-tensix-optimize-dce
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_dce) Init(1)
Remove dead tensix instructions

mtt-tensix-optimize-pressure-schedule
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_pressure_schedule) Init(0)
Schedule allowlisted straight-line SFPU regions to reduce register pressure

mtt-tensix-optimize-latency-schedule
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_latency_schedule) Init(0)
Fill Tensix result-latency bubbles with independent ready SFPU instructions

mtt-tensix-optimize-interlock-schedule
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_interlock_schedule) Init(0)
Fill audited transparent hardware-interlock stalls with independent SFPU instructions

mtt-tensix-optimize-list-schedule
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_list_schedule) Init(0)
List-schedule audited straight-line SFPU regions over the typed-effect dependence DAG against the modeled issue timeline (latency-shadow filling and independent-chain interleaving; post-allocation, where the eight hard LREGs and their WAR/WAW edges are themselves the pressure bound); unaudited or effect-unproven instructions bound regions and refuse by name, self-loop and repeated-row shapes defer to capture formation by name, and any schedule without a strict modeled-makespan decrease keeps the original order byte-identically

mtt-tensix-optimize-capture-rotation
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_capture_rotation) Init(0)
Rotate replayed capture rows to fill audited interlock stalls across the row boundary

mtt-tensix-optimize-drain-schedule
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_drain_schedule) Init(0)
Prove per-boundary macro-event drain requirements from the derived descriptor calendars and elide structurally multiplied drain NOPs at proven-neutral macro run boundaries (refusals keep the full derived drain byte-identically)

mtt-tensix-optimize-init-hoist
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_init_hoist) Init(0)
Hoist a noinline callee's loop-invariant idempotent macro-planner init prefix (the derived descriptor program, and where the caller's reaching configuration is proven value-equal, the owned SETC16 program and all-lanes enable) into the proven caller's loop preheader, executing it once per loop instead of once per call; every unproven link refuses by name and keeps the per-call prefix byte-identically.

mtt-tensix-optimize-prgm-const
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_prgm_const) Init(0)
Allocate programmable constant registers to loop-invariant SFPU immediates

mtt-tensix-optimize-const-residency
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_const_residency) Init(0)
Allocate programmable constant registers to proven-constant SFPU values by priced selection, in-loop materializations first

mtt-tensix-optimize-const-remat
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_const_remat) Init(0)
Rematerialize proven loadi-materialized SFPU values at their uses when vector register pressure exceeds the LREG file

mtt-tensix-optimize-lreg-alloc
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_lreg_alloc) Init(0)
When SFPU vector pressure exceeds the 8-register LREG file, DSATUR-color the interference graph before IRA and spill selected vector webs through proven-free 32-bit Dst scratch rows (SFPSTORE/SFPLOAD round trip) until the graph is 8-colorable; assignment stays with IRA, every unproven ingredient refuses by name, and the lreg-pressure-exceeded error is kept byte-identically on refusal

mtt-tensix-dst-layout-32b
Target Var(riscv_tt_dst_layout_32b) Init(0)
Integration-layer declaration that every SFPU calc body in this translation unit executes under a 32-bit-row Dst layout (fp32 dest accumulation / 32-bit dest addressing); consumed by -mtt-tensix-optimize-lreg-alloc to admit runtime-resolved (SRCB mode 0) and Dst-untouched kernels for scratch-row spilling. DECLARING THIS FALSELY ON A 16-BIT-LAYOUT KERNEL MAKES A SPILLED COMPILATION PRODUCE SILENT WRONG OUTPUT (no run-time error exists); the build layer must set it from the kernel's dest-accumulation mode. Affirmative 16-bit-format accesses refuse regardless of this declaration

mtt-tensix-optimize-transp-involution
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_transp_involution) Init(0)
Fuse a Tensix SFPTRANSP with the full-bank loads defining its operands into one companion-preserving involution bundle, and forward proven-identity Dst parks across it.

mtt-tensix-optimize-replay-exec-record
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_replay_exec_record) Init(0)
Execute a hoisted Tensix replay capture while recording and drop the first now-redundant playback launch when the unrolled launch run structurally proves the exchange.

mtt-tensix-optimize-dst-iteration-fusion
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_dst_iteration_fusion) Init(0)
Recognize legal adjacent Tensix Dst-register iterations

mtt-tensix-optimize-lp-schedule
Target Undocumented Alias(mtt-tensix-optimize-pressure-schedule)

mtt-tensix-pressure-schedule-use-milp
Target Var(riscv_tt_pressure_schedule_use_milp) Init(0)
Use the built-in exact branch-and-bound solver for Tensix pressure scheduling when the list schedule cannot satisfy capacity (--with-lp-solve builds also cross-check it against lp_solve).

mtt-tensix-optimize-replay
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_replay) Init(1)
Generate Tensix replay instruction.

mtt-tensix-optimize-replay-hoist
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_replay_hoist) Init(0)
Hoist fixed-encoding Tensix replay capture out of profitable loops.

mtt-tensix-optimize-counted-row-formation
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_counted_row) Init(0)
Canonicalize parameterized repeated Tensix SFPU rows (immediate-varying members excluded from the record and delivered between launches; clone register maps rewritten to the recorded registers) so replay formation records one parameterized row program.

mtt-tensix-optimize-replay-loop-unroll
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_replay_loop_unroll) Init(0)
Request generic loop unrolling for counted single-block Tensix SFPU row loops whose every statement is a typed SFPU builtin, so the existing replay formation can capture the repeated row (default off).

mtt-tensix-replay-hoist-min-benefit=
Target Joined RejectNegative UInteger Var(riscv_tt_replay_hoist_min_benefit) Init(-1)
Minimum modeled benefit, in hundredths of an issue slot, required to hoist a replay capture; overrides the target cost-table default.

mtt-tensix-optimize-mop-form
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_mop_form) Init(0)
Re-roll runs and counted loops of identical Tensix replay playback launches into a hardware MOP loop.

mtt-tensix-mop-form-min-benefit=
Target Joined RejectNegative UInteger Var(riscv_tt_mop_form_min_benefit) Init(-1)
Minimum modeled benefit, in hundredths of an issue slot, required to form a MOP loop; overrides the target cost-table default.

mtt-tensix-mop-form-force
Target Var(riscv_tt_mop_form_force) Init(0)
Testing and measurement only: bypass the MOP formation profitability refusal (every structural, ownership, and buffer proof still applies), to build silicon A/B legs for shapes the corrected delivery model prices as non-winning.

mtt-tensix-optimize-invariant-loadi
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_invariant_loadi) Init(0)
Hoist loop-invariant Tensix immediate-vector materialization before register allocation.

mtt-tensix-optimize-dst-autoincr
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_dst_autoincr) Init(0)
Replace constant-stride per-row Dst RWC increments with owned address-modifier auto-increment.

mtt-tensix-optimize-dst-ownership
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_dst_ownership) Init(1)
Default-on (promoted after silicon validation; disable with -mno-tt-tensix-optimize-dst-ownership): fold proven-identity Dst reloads into LREG-resident values using the pre-IRA Dst/RWC ownership analysis.

mtt-tensix-optimize-lut-select
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_lut_select) Init(1)
Default-on (promoted after silicon validation; disable with -mno-tt-tensix-optimize-lut-select): select Tensix SFPU LUT instructions from encodable magnitude range-dispatch trees.

mtt-tensix-optimize-lut-select-leaf-ext
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_lut_select_leaf_ext) Init(0)
Default-off: extend LUT instruction selection with certified non-affine leaf classes (multiply-only leaves, provable-constant leaves) and below-arity partition duplication; admission per slot is the exhaustive bit-exact certification recorded in rvtt-lut-tables.cc.

mtt-tensix-optimize-crosscall-hoist
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_crosscall_hoist) Init(0)
Hoist a noinline callee's call-invariant pinned-LREG immediate materializations (the LUT coefficient prefix) into every proven caller's loop preheader, carrying the values across calls in the architecturally pinned hard LREGs; every unproven link refuses by name.

mtt-tensix-optimize-crossloop-hoist
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_crossloop_hoist) Init(0)
Hoist loop-invariant SFPU immediate materializations (and, with the programmable-constant passes, their SFPCONFIG programming points) across enclosing loops whose bodies deliver only audited-inert instruction words (raw .ttinsn constants, instruction-FIFO stores, MOPs with a proven TU template census); every unaudited word or statement class refuses by name.

mtt-tensix-optimize-repr-prop
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_repr_prop) Init(0)
Cancel Tensix SFPU representation-conversion pairs (audited bit involutions, e.g. the BH sign-magnitude/two's-complement cast) across value webs that only lanewise choose bits (control joins, predicated live-value merges, copies); any unaudited conversion, non-transparent consumer, or unproven web leaf refuses by name.

mtt-tensix-optimize-lreg-rename
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_lreg_rename) Init(0)
Rename storage-colliding invariant-input LREG chains inside capturable rows to a proven-free register so the audited stall-fill mechanisms stop refusing them; every unproven case refuses by name.

mtt-tensix-optimize-ccmask
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_ccmask) Init(0)
Fold a single-zero-assign Tensix SFPU CC region (predicated zeroing under a float order test against +0.0) into a value-mask compare and AND; misses refuse by name and keep the CC lowering byte-identically.

mtt-tensix-optimize-int-abs
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_int_abs) Init(0)
Fold a conditional-negate Tensix SFPU CC region (predicated two's-complement negation under a signed-int sign test against 0) into the single integer SFPABS, per the shipped exhaustive equivalence proof; misses refuse by name and keep the CC lowering byte-identically.

mtt-tensix-optimize-int-not
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_int_not) Init(0)
Select the single SFPNOT for the all-ones-minus-x one's-complement value function, per the shipped exhaustive equivalence proof; misses refuse by name and keep the subtract byte-identically.

mtt-tensix-optimize-store-fold
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_store_fold) Init(0)
Fold a lane-predicated SFPU value merge into its consuming Dst store: forward the merge source into a same-mask store, and sink a post-region store into the region as a predicated store where the format pair's Dst round trip is proven the identity; every unproven case refuses by name.

mtt-tensix-optimize-setexp-fold
Target Var(riscv_tt_opt_setexp_fold) Init(1)
Default-on (promoted after silicon validation; disable with -mno-tt-tensix-optimize-setexp-fold): fold a biased Tensix SFPU exponent extract feeding SFPSETEXP into the exponent-copy addressing mode.

mtt-tensix-analyze-loadmacro
Target Var(riscv_tt_analyze_loadmacro) Init(0)
Removed with the quarantined exact-calendar SFPLOADMACRO pass (WP8); errors on use.

mtt-tensix-emit-loadmacro
Target Var(riscv_tt_emit_loadmacro) Init(0)
Removed with the quarantined exact-calendar SFPLOADMACRO pass (WP8); errors on use.

mtt-tensix-macro-planner
Target Var(riscv_tt_macro_planner) Init(0)
Default-off: plan, prove, and materialize SFPLOADMACRO schedules from typed effects and target capability tables.

mtt-tensix-macro-planner-analyze
Target Var(riscv_tt_macro_planner_analyze) Init(0)
Discover, prove, and report generic macro-planner regions and named refusals without changing code.

mtt-tensix-macro-planner-verify
Target Var(riscv_tt_macro_planner_verify) Init(0)
Differentially verify synthesized macro-planner descriptors against the region's explicit facts (also forced on under internal checking).

mtt-tensix-macro-planner-verify-corrupt-template
Target Var(riscv_tt_macro_planner_verify_corrupt_template) Init(0)
Testing only: corrupt the verifier's local copy of the first synthesized template word before Layer-7 comparison, pinning that a verification mismatch refuses formation.  Never touches the descriptor itself.

mtt-tensix-macro-planner-replay
Target Var(riscv_tt_macro_planner_replay) Init(0)
Default-off delivery increment: admit planner-formed SFPLOADMACRO launches into automatic replay recording (the launch is a pure instruction word; execution at a replay site reads the then-current descriptor configuration, matching the production handwritten Where kernel's own recorded launches).  Off keeps every planner-formed calendar byte-identical to the pre-flag output.

mtt-tensix-macro-planner-residency
Target Var(riscv_tt_macro_planner_residency) Init(0)
Default-off delivery increment: descriptor-program residency for the macro planner.  Extends the proven cross-tile configuration epoch outward through successively enclosing loops (the programming words become resident once per kernel entry instead of once per enclosing-loop trip), and elides the descriptor-word programming of a later region whose derived descriptor words are bit-identical to an already-programmed dominating one (content-equality de-duplication; the per-region ambient enable and owned SETC16 program always stay).  Every proof failure refuses by a stable name and keeps today's placement byte-identically.

mtt-tensix-macro-ims
Target Var(riscv_tt_macro_ims) Init(0)
Default-off placement increment (WP13): iterative-modulo-scheduling repair over the macro sub-unit calendar -- when the maximal hosting proposal refuses downstream, deterministically retry with reduced hosted sets (Rau-style bounded unplacement) instead of refusing the whole region -- plus delivery-model formation-vs-replay arbitration: formation additionally requires the formed calendar to price below the replay-compressed explicit alternative under the shared issue-cost model.  Off keeps every schedule candidate and formation decision byte-identical to the pre-flag output.

mtt-tensix-macro-ims-carrier
Target Var(riscv_tt_macro_ims_carrier) Init(0)
Default-off placement increment (WP15, the upward half of the WP14 IMS mapping): extra-value-carrier formation for the macro planner.  When the established (and, under -mtt-tensix-macro-ims, repaired) search proves a formed calendar, deterministically enumerate re-load carrier variants -- duplicate one of the row's proven no-increment Dst loads into a provably free LREG, replicate its in-place cooking prefix, and version-split-rename one explicit consumer web onto the new carrier -- applied by commit-or-revert mutation across every unrolled row copy.  A variant commits only when the mutated region re-proves through the full derivation pipeline at a strictly smaller initiation interval and passes every established formation gate; otherwise the mutation reverts byte-identically under a stable refusal name.  Off keeps every schedule and formation decision byte-identical to the pre-flag output.

mtt-tensix-dump-effects
Target Var(riscv_tt_dump_effects) Init(0)
Annotate assembler output with the generated Tensix architectural effect set of each instruction (debug/self-check aid).

mtt-tensix-replay-buffer-size=
Target Joined RejectNegative Var(riscv_tt_replay_size) UInteger Init(32) IntegerRange(1,32)
Length of replay buffer for replay optimization use.

